WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.997
A source review becomes more useful when we quantify the problems.

00:00:03.997 --> 00:00:05.997
How many values are missing?

00:00:05.997 --> 00:00:08.292
How many fail a validation rule?

00:00:08.292 --> 00:00:13.872
How many duplicate groups appear after normalization?

00:00:13.872 --> 00:00:16.652
Are unusual values rare but plausible, or clearly impossible?

00:00:16.652 --> 00:00:23.942
Profiling gives you a baseline and helps you measure whether a cleaning step actually improves the dataset.

00:00:23.942 --> 00:00:30.042
Connect this idea to a product catalog standardizing categories and quarantining invalid rows.

00:00:30.042 --> 00:00:37.802
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:37.802 --> 00:00:43.667
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:49.617
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:49.617 --> 00:00:55.520
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
